 zip(vec, query_vector))\n        norm_vec = math.sqrt(sum(a*a for a in vec))\n        norm_query = math.sqrt(sum(b*b for b in query_vector))\n        if norm_vec == 0.0 or norm_query == 0.0:\n            sims.append(0.0)\n        else:\n            sims.append(dot / (norm_vec * norm_query))\n    \n    # For each position, average neighbor similarities\n    blended = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        own = sims[i]\n        neighbor_sims = []\n        if i > 0:\n            neighbor_sims.append(sims[i-1])\n        if i < n-1:\n            neighbor_sims.append(sims[i+1])\n        neighbor_avg = sum(neighbor_sims) / len(neighbor_sims) if neighbor_sims else 0.0\n        blend = own * (1 - context_weight) + neighbor_avg * context_weight\n        # Round to 6 decimal places\n        blended.append(round(blend, 6))\n    \n    # Rank: descending score, then ascending index\n    indices = list(range(n))\n    indices.sort(key=lambda i: (-blended[i], i))\n    ranking = indices\n    scores = [blended[i] for i in ranking]\n    \n    return {\n        'ranking': ranking,\n        'scores': scores\n    }\n```\n\nBut need to handle case where case may have missing fields? The spec says validate every required field before computing. So we should check that all required fields exist. If not, raise ValueError. Also check types? The payload seems consistent. But to be safe, we can check.\n\nAlso note: The field _case_nonce is present but unused.\n\nI'll add validation at start: if not all(k in case for k in ['sentence_vectors','query_vector','context_weight']): raise ValueError(\"Missing required field\").\n\nAlso validate that sentence_vectors is list of lists of numbers, etc. But not strictly required, maybe just rely on runtime errors.\n\nNow produce the JSON output. The code as a string must be escaped. I'll write it carefully.\n\nThe final answer should be a JSON object with key \"implementation\" and value string containing the Python source.\n\nI'll output that."},"logprobs":